# CI test shards (this repo)

Canon: [`.github/workflows/test-suite.yml`](../../.github/workflows/test-suite.yml).
`ci.yml` and `release.yml` **call** that workflow. Do not copy a second `dotnet test` matrix.

The repo is **public** — GitHub-hosted minutes are not the limit (~20 concurrent jobs are).
Do **not** fold CI back into one sequential `dotnet test` on the whole `.sln` to “save runners”.
Wall clock on one Windows job was ~14 minutes because AnalyzerLifecycle is serialized.

## What may not run in one testhost

`[CollectionDefinition("AnalyzerLifecycle", DisableParallelization = true)]` plus
`AnalyzerShadowPublisher`: one MSBuild lifecycle host / shadow dirs. In-process
xUnit threads will race. Unit tests (`Category!=AnalyzerLifecycle`) already parallelize
inside the testhost.

Speedup is **separate GitHub jobs**, not `MaxParallelThreads` on that collection.

## Partition contract

Union of filters must be every discovered test; shards must not overlap.

| Job | Filter |
|---|---|
| `unit` | `Category!=AnalyzerLifecycle` |
| `lifecycle-epoch1` | `Category=AnalyzerLifecycle&FullyQualifiedName~Epoch1` |
| `lifecycle-v3` | `Category=AnalyzerLifecycle&FullyQualifiedName~V3` |
| `lifecycle-epoch4-5` | `Category=AnalyzerLifecycle&(FullyQualifiedName~Epoch4\|FullyQualifiedName~Epoch5)` |
| `lifecycle-rest` | `Category=AnalyzerLifecycle` and **not** Epoch1/V3/Epoch4/Epoch5 |

A new AnalyzerLifecycle class without those name needles **must** land in `lifecycle-rest`.
Do not add a named shard that leaves rest empty without `--filter` proof. Do not drop the rest shard.

`fail-fast: false`. Skip (`AnalyzerLifecycleFact` when the host cannot start) is a **job failure**
(`.github/scripts/Assert-NoSkippedTests.ps1`), not a green CI.

Pass `--filter` as a quoted env value (`"$env:FILTER"`). Bare `&` in PowerShell is the call operator.

JS actions must be Node 24 majors (`checkout@v6`, `setup-dotnet@v5`, `upload-artifact@v7`,
`download-artifact@v8`). Do not pin `@v4` of those — GitHub removes Node 20. Do not set
`ACTIONS_ALLOW_USE_UNSECURE_NODE_VERSION`. Hosted `windows-latest` is new enough.
